{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.2.cb94f54767","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":2,"group":"syn-s-47","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>Dmitri Mensah is a geologist.</li><li>Mensah wanted to find out whether a hillside's plant cover affects how much soil washes away in heavy rain.</li><li>Mensah measured soil runoff on bare slopes and on slopes covered with native grasses.</li><li>Mensah found that bare slopes lost several times more soil.</li><li>Mensah concluded that plant cover may protect hillsides from erosion.</li></ul><p>The student wants to present the study's finding.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["Mensah found that bare slopes lost several times more soil.","Mensah concluded that plant cover may protect hillsides from erosion.","To investigate the question, Mensah measured soil runoff on bare slopes and on slopes covered with native grasses.","Geologist Dmitri Mensah set out to learn whether a hillside's plant cover affects how much soil washes away in heavy rain."],"answer":"A","explanation":"It reports what the researcher observed. A conclusion is an interpretation of a finding, not the finding itself."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.2.6bf9f47ffa","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":2,"group":"syn-s-66","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>Tomás Abara is a linguist.</li><li>Abara wanted to find out whether bilingual children are better at switching between tasks.</li><li>Abara gave bilingual and monolingual children a game that required switching rules quickly.</li><li>Abara found that bilingual children switched rules with fewer errors.</li><li>Abara concluded that speaking two languages may strengthen certain mental skills.</li></ul><p>The student wants to describe how the study was conducted.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["Linguist Tomás Abara set out to learn whether bilingual children are better at switching between tasks.","Abara concluded that speaking two languages may strengthen certain mental skills.","To investigate the question, Abara gave bilingual and monolingual children a game that required switching rules quickly.","Abara found that bilingual children switched rules with fewer errors."],"answer":"C","explanation":"It explains the procedure. The others give the study's aim, finding, or conclusion."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.2.53eca7c480","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":2,"group":"syn-s-71","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>Leila Delacroix is a linguist.</li><li>Delacroix wanted to find out whether bilingual children are better at switching between tasks.</li><li>Delacroix gave bilingual and monolingual children a game that required switching rules quickly.</li><li>Delacroix found that bilingual children switched rules with fewer errors.</li><li>Delacroix concluded that speaking two languages may strengthen certain mental skills.</li></ul><p>The student wants to describe how the study was conducted.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["To investigate the question, Delacroix gave bilingual and monolingual children a game that required switching rules quickly.","Delacroix concluded that speaking two languages may strengthen certain mental skills.","Delacroix found that bilingual children switched rules with fewer errors.","Linguist Leila Delacroix set out to learn whether bilingual children are better at switching between tasks."],"answer":"A","explanation":"It explains the procedure. The others give the study's aim, finding, or conclusion."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.2.1c91b19888","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":2,"group":"syn-s-80","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>Kenji Varga is a botanist.</li><li>Varga wanted to find out whether tomato plants grow better with music played nearby.</li><li>Varga grew tomato plants in two identical greenhouses, one with music and one without.</li><li>Varga found that plants in both greenhouses grew at similar rates.</li><li>Varga concluded that music may have little effect on tomato growth.</li></ul><p>The student wants to describe how the study was conducted.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["To investigate the question, Varga grew tomato plants in two identical greenhouses, one with music and one without.","Varga found that plants in both greenhouses grew at similar rates.","Botanist Kenji Varga set out to learn whether tomato plants grow better with music played nearby.","Varga concluded that music may have little effect on tomato growth."],"answer":"A","explanation":"It explains the procedure. The others give the study's aim, finding, or conclusion."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.2.85be056372","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":2,"group":"syn-s-86","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>Idris Oyelaran is an urban planner.</li><li>Oyelaran wanted to find out whether adding trees along streets lowers summer temperatures.</li><li>Oyelaran measured afternoon temperatures on streets with and without tree cover.</li><li>Oyelaran found that streets with trees were up to four degrees cooler.</li><li>Oyelaran concluded that street trees may help cities stay cooler in summer.</li></ul><p>The student wants to describe how the study was conducted.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["Oyelaran found that streets with trees were up to four degrees cooler.","To investigate the question, Oyelaran measured afternoon temperatures on streets with and without tree cover.","Urban planner Idris Oyelaran set out to learn whether adding trees along streets lowers summer temperatures.","Oyelaran concluded that street trees may help cities stay cooler in summer."],"answer":"B","explanation":"It explains the procedure. The others give the study's aim, finding, or conclusion."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.2.32618089b0","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":2,"group":"syn-s-87","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>Kwame Mensah is an urban planner.</li><li>Mensah wanted to find out whether adding trees along streets lowers summer temperatures.</li><li>Mensah measured afternoon temperatures on streets with and without tree cover.</li><li>Mensah found that streets with trees were up to four degrees cooler.</li><li>Mensah concluded that street trees may help cities stay cooler in summer.</li></ul><p>The student wants to describe how the study was conducted.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["Urban planner Kwame Mensah set out to learn whether adding trees along streets lowers summer temperatures.","Mensah concluded that street trees may help cities stay cooler in summer.","To investigate the question, Mensah measured afternoon temperatures on streets with and without tree cover.","Mensah found that streets with trees were up to four degrees cooler."],"answer":"C","explanation":"It explains the procedure. The others give the study's aim, finding, or conclusion."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.2.0ec6526752","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":2,"group":"syn-s-88","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>Elias Moreau is an urban planner.</li><li>Moreau wanted to find out whether adding trees along streets lowers summer temperatures.</li><li>Moreau measured afternoon temperatures on streets with and without tree cover.</li><li>Moreau found that streets with trees were up to four degrees cooler.</li><li>Moreau concluded that street trees may help cities stay cooler in summer.</li></ul><p>The student wants to describe how the study was conducted.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["Moreau concluded that street trees may help cities stay cooler in summer.","Moreau found that streets with trees were up to four degrees cooler.","Urban planner Elias Moreau set out to learn whether adding trees along streets lowers summer temperatures.","To investigate the question, Moreau measured afternoon temperatures on streets with and without tree cover."],"answer":"D","explanation":"It explains the procedure. The others give the study's aim, finding, or conclusion."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.2.9a9b355042","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":2,"group":"syn-s-89","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>Sofia Moreau is an urban planner.</li><li>Moreau wanted to find out whether adding trees along streets lowers summer temperatures.</li><li>Moreau measured afternoon temperatures on streets with and without tree cover.</li><li>Moreau found that streets with trees were up to four degrees cooler.</li><li>Moreau concluded that street trees may help cities stay cooler in summer.</li></ul><p>The student wants to describe how the study was conducted.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["Moreau found that streets with trees were up to four degrees cooler.","Urban planner Sofia Moreau set out to learn whether adding trees along streets lowers summer temperatures.","Moreau concluded that street trees may help cities stay cooler in summer.","To investigate the question, Moreau measured afternoon temperatures on streets with and without tree cover."],"answer":"D","explanation":"It explains the procedure. The others give the study's aim, finding, or conclusion."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.2.00e6adf9c4","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":2,"group":"syn-s-91","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>Mei Halvorsen is a hydrologist.</li><li>Halvorsen wanted to find out whether wetlands reduce flooding downstream.</li><li>Halvorsen compared river levels below restored wetlands with levels below drained farmland after storms.</li><li>Halvorsen found that river levels rose more slowly below the wetlands.</li><li>Halvorsen concluded that wetlands may help protect nearby communities from floods.</li></ul><p>The student wants to present the study's finding.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["To investigate the question, Halvorsen compared river levels below restored wetlands with levels below drained farmland after storms.","Halvorsen concluded that wetlands may help protect nearby communities from floods.","Halvorsen found that river levels rose more slowly below the wetlands.","Hydrologist Mei Halvorsen set out to learn whether wetlands reduce flooding downstream."],"answer":"C","explanation":"It reports what the researcher observed. A conclusion is an interpretation of a finding, not the finding itself."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.2.b99b81128d","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":2,"group":"syn-s-104","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>Jonas Duarte is a chemist.</li><li>Duarte wanted to find out whether a new plant-based plastic breaks down in seawater.</li><li>Duarte placed samples of the plastic in tanks of seawater for six months.</li><li>Duarte found that most samples broke apart within four months.</li><li>Duarte concluded that the plastic may be less harmful to oceans than conventional plastic.</li></ul><p>The student wants to present the study's finding.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["Duarte found that most samples broke apart within four months.","Chemist Jonas Duarte set out to learn whether a new plant-based plastic breaks down in seawater.","Duarte concluded that the plastic may be less harmful to oceans than conventional plastic.","To investigate the question, Duarte placed samples of the plastic in tanks of seawater for six months."],"answer":"A","explanation":"It reports what the researcher observed. A conclusion is an interpretation of a finding, not the finding itself."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.2.d2cc3226bb","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":2,"group":"syn-s-109","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>Lucía Petrov is a primatologist.</li><li>Petrov wanted to find out whether young chimpanzees learn to use tools by watching adults.</li><li>Petrov observed young chimpanzees in groups where adults cracked nuts with stones and in groups where adults did not.</li><li>Petrov found that young chimpanzees in the nut-cracking groups began using stones much earlier.</li><li>Petrov concluded that young chimpanzees may learn tool use by observation.</li></ul><p>The student wants to present the study's finding.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["Primatologist Lucía Petrov set out to learn whether young chimpanzees learn to use tools by watching adults.","Petrov found that young chimpanzees in the nut-cracking groups began using stones much earlier.","To investigate the question, Petrov observed young chimpanzees in groups where adults cracked nuts with stones and in groups where adults did not.","Petrov concluded that young chimpanzees may learn tool use by observation."],"answer":"B","explanation":"It reports what the researcher observed. A conclusion is an interpretation of a finding, not the finding itself."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.2.c04e364939","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":2,"group":"syn-s-111","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>Tomás Takeda is a primatologist.</li><li>Takeda wanted to find out whether young chimpanzees learn to use tools by watching adults.</li><li>Takeda observed young chimpanzees in groups where adults cracked nuts with stones and in groups where adults did not.</li><li>Takeda found that young chimpanzees in the nut-cracking groups began using stones much earlier.</li><li>Takeda concluded that young chimpanzees may learn tool use by observation.</li></ul><p>The student wants to describe how the study was conducted.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["Takeda found that young chimpanzees in the nut-cracking groups began using stones much earlier.","Takeda concluded that young chimpanzees may learn tool use by observation.","To investigate the question, Takeda observed young chimpanzees in groups where adults cracked nuts with stones and in groups where adults did not.","Primatologist Tomás Takeda set out to learn whether young chimpanzees learn to use tools by watching adults."],"answer":"C","explanation":"It explains the procedure. The others give the study's aim, finding, or conclusion."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.2.fa1b8deaef","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":2,"group":"syn-s-112","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>Samuel Adeyemi is a primatologist.</li><li>Adeyemi wanted to find out whether young chimpanzees learn to use tools by watching adults.</li><li>Adeyemi observed young chimpanzees in groups where adults cracked nuts with stones and in groups where adults did not.</li><li>Adeyemi found that young chimpanzees in the nut-cracking groups began using stones much earlier.</li><li>Adeyemi concluded that young chimpanzees may learn tool use by observation.</li></ul><p>The student wants to describe how the study was conducted.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["Adeyemi concluded that young chimpanzees may learn tool use by observation.","Primatologist Samuel Adeyemi set out to learn whether young chimpanzees learn to use tools by watching adults.","Adeyemi found that young chimpanzees in the nut-cracking groups began using stones much earlier.","To investigate the question, Adeyemi observed young chimpanzees in groups where adults cracked nuts with stones and in groups where adults did not."],"answer":"D","explanation":"It explains the procedure. The others give the study's aim, finding, or conclusion."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.2.77e73c6b45","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":2,"group":"syn-s-116","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>Tomás Ferreira is a sleep researcher.</li><li>Ferreira wanted to find out whether using screens before bed affects how quickly people fall asleep.</li><li>Ferreira asked volunteers to read either a printed book or a tablet for an hour before bed.</li><li>Ferreira found that tablet readers took about ten minutes longer to fall asleep.</li><li>Ferreira concluded that screen use before bed may delay sleep.</li></ul><p>The student wants to present the study's finding.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["Ferreira concluded that screen use before bed may delay sleep.","Ferreira found that tablet readers took about ten minutes longer to fall asleep.","Sleep researcher Tomás Ferreira set out to learn whether using screens before bed affects how quickly people fall asleep.","To investigate the question, Ferreira asked volunteers to read either a printed book or a tablet for an hour before bed."],"answer":"B","explanation":"It reports what the researcher observed. A conclusion is an interpretation of a finding, not the finding itself."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.2.11f3c9a1b0","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":2,"group":"syn-s-124","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>Ayumi Quintero is an ornithologist.</li><li>Quintero wanted to find out whether birds that migrate farther have longer wings.</li><li>Quintero measured the wings of several related species with different migration distances.</li><li>Quintero found that species that migrated farther tended to have longer, narrower wings.</li><li>Quintero concluded that wing shape may be linked to migration distance.</li></ul><p>The student wants to describe how the study was conducted.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["To investigate the question, Quintero measured the wings of several related species with different migration distances.","Quintero concluded that wing shape may be linked to migration distance.","Quintero found that species that migrated farther tended to have longer, narrower wings.","Ornithologist Ayumi Quintero set out to learn whether birds that migrate farther have longer wings."],"answer":"A","explanation":"It explains the procedure. The others give the study's aim, finding, or conclusion."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.2.397bbfb0cf","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":2,"group":"syn-s-127","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>Kofi Duarte is a public health researcher.</li><li>Duarte wanted to find out whether adding bike lanes increases how often residents cycle.</li><li>Duarte counted cyclists on streets before and after new bike lanes were added.</li><li>Duarte found that cycling on those streets nearly doubled within a year.</li><li>Duarte concluded that bike lanes may encourage more people to ride.</li></ul><p>The student wants to present the study's finding.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["Public health researcher Kofi Duarte set out to learn whether adding bike lanes increases how often residents cycle.","To investigate the question, Duarte counted cyclists on streets before and after new bike lanes were added.","Duarte found that cycling on those streets nearly doubled within a year.","Duarte concluded that bike lanes may encourage more people to ride."],"answer":"C","explanation":"It reports what the researcher observed. A conclusion is an interpretation of a finding, not the finding itself."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.2.a2d667daf4","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":2,"group":"syn-s-141","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>Ravi Sato is a neuroscientist.</li><li>Sato wanted to find out whether learning to juggle changes brain structure.</li><li>Sato scanned volunteers' brains before and after three months of juggling practice.</li><li>Sato found that regions linked to tracking movement grew slightly larger.</li><li>Sato concluded that practicing a new skill may reshape parts of the brain.</li></ul><p>The student wants to present the study's finding.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["Sato found that regions linked to tracking movement grew slightly larger.","Neuroscientist Ravi Sato set out to learn whether learning to juggle changes brain structure.","To investigate the question, Sato scanned volunteers' brains before and after three months of juggling practice.","Sato concluded that practicing a new skill may reshape parts of the brain."],"answer":"A","explanation":"It reports what the researcher observed. A conclusion is an interpretation of a finding, not the finding itself."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.2.83e3b184fe","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":2,"group":"syn-s-142","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>Zara Sato is a neuroscientist.</li><li>Sato wanted to find out whether learning to juggle changes brain structure.</li><li>Sato scanned volunteers' brains before and after three months of juggling practice.</li><li>Sato found that regions linked to tracking movement grew slightly larger.</li><li>Sato concluded that practicing a new skill may reshape parts of the brain.</li></ul><p>The student wants to describe how the study was conducted.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["To investigate the question, Sato scanned volunteers' brains before and after three months of juggling practice.","Neuroscientist Zara Sato set out to learn whether learning to juggle changes brain structure.","Sato concluded that practicing a new skill may reshape parts of the brain.","Sato found that regions linked to tracking movement grew slightly larger."],"answer":"A","explanation":"It explains the procedure. The others give the study's aim, finding, or conclusion."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.2.cffa9cdbc7","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":2,"group":"syn-s-171","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>Priya Varga is a forest ecologist.</li><li>Varga wanted to find out whether fungi help trees share nutrients.</li><li>Varga added a traceable form of carbon to some trees and checked nearby trees for it.</li><li>Varga found that the carbon appeared in neighboring trees connected by fungal networks.</li><li>Varga concluded that fungal networks may move nutrients between trees.</li></ul><p>The student wants to describe how the study was conducted.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["Varga found that the carbon appeared in neighboring trees connected by fungal networks.","Varga concluded that fungal networks may move nutrients between trees.","To investigate the question, Varga added a traceable form of carbon to some trees and checked nearby trees for it.","Forest ecologist Priya Varga set out to learn whether fungi help trees share nutrients."],"answer":"C","explanation":"It explains the procedure. The others give the study's aim, finding, or conclusion."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.2.eee4da7661","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":2,"group":"syn-s-177","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>Zara Vance is a music researcher.</li><li>Vance wanted to find out whether learning an instrument improves children's listening skills.</li><li>Vance tested children's ability to pick out sounds in noise before and after two years of music lessons.</li><li>Vance found that children who took lessons improved more than those who did not.</li><li>Vance concluded that music training may sharpen listening skills.</li></ul><p>The student wants to describe how the study was conducted.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["Vance concluded that music training may sharpen listening skills.","To investigate the question, Vance tested children's ability to pick out sounds in noise before and after two years of music lessons.","Music researcher Zara Vance set out to learn whether learning an instrument improves children's listening skills.","Vance found that children who took lessons improved more than those who did not."],"answer":"B","explanation":"It explains the procedure. The others give the study's aim, finding, or conclusion."}
